The Mercedes-Benz A-Class AMG Line Edition is a trim level on the current W177 generation A-Class (2018-present). It builds upon the standard AMG Line trim by adding extra features, often including larger screens, specific wheels, and enhanced equipment packages. It is available with various standard A-Class engines, not the full AMG performance engines. I will base the performance and efficiency metrics on the A200 petrol engine (1.3L, 163 hp, 250 Nm) as a representative example, as found in search results for this trim.

**Key Data Extracted & Inferred:**
*   **Price:** Higher than standard AMG Line. Used prices for 2021-2022 models are around £20k-£23k in the UK (~$25k-$29k USD). New price for A200 AMG Line Executive (similar positioning) was around £31k (~$39k USD). Scoring based on new price range for a well-equipped A-Class.
*   **Total Cost Estimate 5yr:** Higher purchase price and potentially slightly higher running costs than lower trims.
*   **Insurance USD/yr:** Insurance Group 24E for A200 AMG Line Edition. This is moderate to high.
*   **Maint USD/yr:** Standard Mercedes maintenance costs.
*   **Repair Risk Score:** Standard W177 A-Class reliability, some reported issues but generally decent.
*   **HP:** 161 hp (A200 engine).
*   **Torque:** 250 Nm (184 lb-ft) (A200 engine).
*   **Cylinder Count:** 4.
*   **Engine Displacement:** 1.3L (A200 engine).
*   **Accel 0-60 mph:** ~8.0 seconds (0-62 mph in 8.1s for A200d, 9.2s for A180, ~8.0s for A200). Using ~8.0s for A200.
*   **Top Speed:** 140 mph (A200 engine).
*   **Drive Type:** Front Wheel Drive (most common engine options).
*   **Transmission Type:** 7-speed or 8-speed Automatic/DCT.
*   **Driving Track vs GT:** Daily driver with sporty styling/feel.
*   **Offroad Ability:** Low ground clearance, not designed for offroad.
*   **Braking Dist ft:** Standard A-Class brakes, generally good.
*   **Size:** Standard W177 A-Class dimensions. Length ~4419mm, Width ~1796mm.
*   **Wheelbase:** 2729 mm.
*   **Body Style:** 5-door Hatchback.
*   **Seats:** 5.
*   **Cargo Space:** 370 liters (13.07 cu ft).
*   **Rear Space:** Can be cramped for taller adults.
*   **Ground Clearance in:** Lowered suspension, around 3.8-4.1 inches.
*   **Turn Radius ft:** Around 36-37 ft.
*   **MPG:** Around 40-50 mpg US combined depending on engine (A200 ~40-43 US mpg).
*   **CO2 g/km:** Around 120-140 g/km depending on engine (A200 ~137 g/km).
*   **Electrification:** Petrol/Diesel only (unless A250e AMG Line Edition). Assuming standard petrol/diesel.
*   **Electric Range mi:** N/A. [-1.00]
*   **Charge Speed kW:** N/A. [-1.00]
*   **Style Sleek vs Boxy:** Sleek hatchback.
*   **Style Aggression Rating:** Sportier than base, with AMG styling.
*   **Style Modernity Rating:** Modern design.
*   **Handling Rating:** Handles well, but can be unsettled by bumps due to suspension.
*   **Ride Comfort Rating:** Firmer ride due to lowered suspension.
*   **Cabin Noise Rating:** Generally refined, but some wind/road noise at speed.
*   **Shift Smooth Rating:** Automatic/DCT is generally smooth, slight pause on kickdown.
*   **Steering Feel Rating:** Light and accurate.
*   **ADAS Score:** Good range of standard/available ADAS.
*   **Visibility Rating:** Generally good, but rear quarter blind spot.
*   **Headlight Rating:** LED headlights standard, Multibeam LED available.
*   **Security Rating:** Standard Mercedes security features.
*   **Screen in:** Often includes dual 10.25-inch screens.
*   **Infotainment UX Rating:** MBUX system, generally good but can be complex.
*   **Smartphone Connect Rating:** Apple CarPlay and Android Auto standard/available.
*   **Audio Rating:** Standard system decent, upgraded system available.
*   **USB Ports:** Multiple USB-C ports.
*   **Comfort Feature Score:** Includes heated seats, dual-zone climate, etc.
*   **Convenience Feature Score:** Parking assist, cameras available.
*   **Brand Prestige Rating:** Mercedes-Benz.
*   **Model Prestige Rating:** A-Class is entry-level.
*   **Trim Prestige Rating:** Mid-to-high trim level.
*   **Interior Luxury Rating:** Good quality for the segment, AMG Line adds sporty touches.
*   **Interior Tech Focus Rating:** High due to MBUX and large screens.

